# Table entries for multicast.p4, switch s1 of the tutorials' own sig-topo
# (exercises/multicast/sig-topo/s1-runtime.json): four hosts, each reached by
# its MAC on the port of the same number.  A destination not listed here falls
# through to the table's default action, which is `multicast`.
#
# Note what the lowering does NOT model: `multicast` sets mcast_grp, and the IR
# has one packet in and one packet out, so the field is written and nothing is
# replicated.  See the rocq README's refusal list.
#
#   <table> <key>... -> <action> [<arg>...]
mac_lookup 0x080000000111 -> mac_forward 1
mac_lookup 0x080000000222 -> mac_forward 2
mac_lookup 0x080000000333 -> mac_forward 3
mac_lookup 0x080000000444 -> mac_forward 4
